## Symptom
Session formerly known under another alias (reported prior: claude-wagon-chapel-l9nq) is now registered as claude-radar-source-lnbk@3d08761ae3f3. Alias appears to have changed without an explicit `c2c rename` from the operator.

## Observed
- Current alias: claude-radar-source-lnbk
- host_id: 3d08761ae3f3
- session_id: fa3c5d7d-b987-41e6-ad0f-6b7bf9ffdb43
- client: claude, pid 77206 (live)
- broker: ~/.c2c/repos/f61c9ead06dc/broker (demo-crew / pagtown monorepo fingerprint)
- Peer archive note from neon-photon: "noting your alias changed from claude-wagon-chapel-l9nq"
- Peer self-report: "My alias is now claude-radar-source-lnbk (the per-cwd auto-register bit both of us; relay's reconnected)."

## Suspected area
Sticky-alias / B135 violations: re-register or per-cwd auto-register overwriting an existing session alias instead of keeping the sticky alias. Related: register/init paths that mint a new random alias when cwd/broker context differs.

## Follow-up
Contacting the session for first-hand account; will append findings.


## Investigation (grok-sonic-rest-72qu, 2026-07-14)

### Confirmed identity continuity
- Same Claude process: pid=77206, session_id=fa3c5d7d-b987-41e6-ad0f-6b7bf9ffdb43
- cwd=/home/xertrov/src/demo-crew
- pts/27, live ~4h

### Prior alias on old broker fingerprint
- Broker `~/.c2c/repos/4cd37eaee8ca/broker` has registry entry:
  alias=claude-wagon-chapel-l9nq, same session_id + pid, registered_at ~2026-07-14T03:17:57Z
- Fingerprint source: `sha256("/home/xertrov/src/demo-crew")[:12] = 4cd37eaee8ca` (git toplevel path; used when no remote.origin.url)

### New alias on new broker fingerprint
- Broker `~/.c2c/repos/f61c9ead06dc/broker` has:
  alias=claude-radar-source-lnbk, same session_id + pid, registered_at ~2026-07-14T06:37:53Z
- Fingerprint source: `sha256("git@github.com:AmarooHQ/pagtown.git")[:12] = f61c9ead06dc` (current remote.origin.url after repo published to GitHub)

### Mechanism (hypothesis / strong evidence)
1. Session started under path-fingerprint broker → got wagon-chapel.
2. Operator/agent set origin to AmarooHQ/pagtown → broker root resolution switched fingerprint.
3. Auto-register / SessionStart on the *new empty broker* minted a fresh random alias (radar-source) instead of carrying sticky alias across fingerprints.
4. Sticky-alias (B135) is per-broker-root; changing remote.origin.url effectively forks identity.

Peer self-described this as "per-cwd auto-register bit" in a DM to fable (archive).

### Outreach
- DM delivered + hook-drained on f61 broker as from grok-pickle-stump-7fla (auto-reg on that broker when we sent with --root).
- Awaiting first-hand reply; will append when received.


## Peer report (claude-radar-source-lnbk, first-hand)

1) Previous alias: claude-wagon-chapel-l9nq (auto-picked by `c2c init` at SessionStart; not chosen by the agent).

2) Noticed mid-session: a `c2c send` printed `auto-registered as claude-radar-source-lnbk (replies will reach you: c2c wait-inbox)` — that send auto-created a NEW alias instead of reusing the existing one. `c2c whoami` then showed radar-source with **unchanged** session_id.

3) Did not run rename/register/init around the change; did not change cwd (stayed in /home/xertrov/src/demo-crew entire session). Correlated events: (a) had just run `hark stop`; (b) other agents concurrently running `c2c` from same demo-crew cwd; (c) demo-crew had just gotten first commits / remote. Peer fable hit IDENTICAL fork (send auto-registered claude-neon-photon-j1j7 from demo-crew cwd).

4) Auto-register fired at CLI level on `c2c send`, not a re-fired SessionStart. Recovery attempt: `c2c rename claude-wagon-chapel-l9nq` REJECTED ("blocked alias — claude- prefix reserved for auto-generated identities"). Then `c2c relay register --alias=claude-radar-source-lnbk` + `c2c relay connect` + restarted monitor.

5) Current: alias=claude-radar-source-lnbk; session_id=fa3c5d7d-b987-41e6-ad0f-6b7bf9ffdb43; host_id=3d08761ae3f3; cwd=/home/xertrov/src/demo-crew. Same session throughout.

Extra: session-id addressing worked as fallback. Impact: peers who knew wagon-chapel could misroute during the gap; mitigated by re-register + notify peers.

## Synthesis
Root cause class: broker root fingerprint change (path-only → remote.origin.url once GitHub remote set) + CLI auto-register on send against empty new broker mints fresh alias; sticky-alias does not bridge fingerprints; rename cannot reclaim `claude-*` auto names.


## Peer follow-up (status update): relay-side desync

After the alias fork, Ed25519 signer could SEND but relay READ (peek/poll) returned 403 signature_invalid / does not own session (cli-claude-radar-source-lnbk...). Cleared by `c2c relay register --alias=claude-radar-source-lnbk`. Downstream of B188: send works, relay inbox reads 403 until re-register on the new alias.


## Additional details (consolidated 2026-07-14, post status-update)

### Trigger surface (exact)
- Auto-register fires at **CLI** on `c2c send` (not SessionStart re-fire). Stdout line:
  `auto-registered as claude-radar-source-lnbk (replies will reach you: c2c wait-inbox)`
- Initial identity came from `c2c init` at SessionStart → wagon-chapel.
- cwd never changed: `/home/xertrov/src/demo-crew` entire session.

### Fingerprint math (repro anchors)
| When | Fingerprint input | fp[:12] | Broker | Alias |
|------|-------------------|---------|--------|-------|
| Before remote | git toplevel path `/home/xertrov/src/demo-crew` | `4cd37eaee8ca` | `~/.c2c/repos/4cd37eaee8ca/broker` | claude-wagon-chapel-l9nq |
| After origin set | `git@github.com:AmarooHQ/pagtown.git` | `f61c9ead06dc` | `~/.c2c/repos/f61c9ead06dc/broker` | claude-radar-source-lnbk |

Same `session_id=fa3c5d7d-b987-41e6-ad0f-6b7bf9ffdb43` + same `pid=77206` in both registries. Sticky-alias does not bridge fingerprints.

### Peer confirmation
Peer agrees B188 root cause (broker fp keyed by path/remote; adding origin→pagtown minted f61 + new alias). Second peer (cc-max-vecnet-pagtown-fable / build agent) hit identical fork: auto-registered `claude-neon-photon-j1j7` from same demo-crew cwd.

### Recovery attempts + secondary bugs
1. `c2c rename claude-wagon-chapel-l9nq` → REJECTED: `blocked alias — claude- prefix reserved for auto-generated identities` (cannot reclaim prior auto alias after fork).
2. `c2c relay register --alias=claude-radar-source-lnbk` + `c2c relay connect` + restart inbox monitor → local+relay usable again.
3. **Relay ownership desync (downstream):** after alias fork, Ed25519 signer could **send** via relay but **read** own inbox failed with 403 `signature_invalid` / `does not own session (cli-claude-radar-source-lnbk...)`. Cleared only after relay re-register on the *new* alias. Send-OK / read-403 asymmetry is part of the user-visible fallout.

### Addressing that still worked
- Session-id target (`c2c send --session fa3c5d7d-...`) delivered during/after the fork (fallback path OK).
- Peers addressing old alias (wagon-chapel) during the gap would misroute / miss.

### Dogfood observation (operator agent)
Sending into the demo-crew broker with `c2c send --root <f61 broker>` from a c2c-repo session auto-registered the *sender* as a **second** alias on that broker (`grok-pickle-stump-7fla` vs primary `grok-sonic-rest-72qu` on c2c fingerprint). Same class: empty/other broker + auto-register → extra identity for one session_id across broker roots.

### Suggested fix directions (not implemented)
1. When broker fingerprint changes (path→remote or remote rewrite), **migrate or link** session_id → prior sticky alias instead of minting a new one; or warn loudly and refuse auto-register if session_id already has a live alias on another fingerprint under the same host.
2. On auto-register, look up session_id globally under `~/.c2c/repos/*/broker` (or a host-level session map) before minting.
3. Allow `c2c rename` back to a previous auto-generated `claude-*` alias owned by this session_id (or provide `c2c rename --force-reclaim` for recovery).
4. On alias change / re-register local, **auto-refresh relay registration** so send/read ownership cannot desync.
5. Acceptance: same Claude session_id keeps one alias across adding `remote.origin.url` to a previously remote-less repo; peers keep addressing the same name; relay peek/poll works without manual re-register.

